@startuml
!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title Requirement → Plan → Behavior Tickets

rectangle "Requirement\nPersist every requirement" as requirement
rectangle "One Plan Issue\nOwns branch + PR + merge" as plan
rectangle "Ordinary requirement\nOne Ticket" as ordinary
rectangle "Complex requirement\nMultiple behavior Tickets" as complex
rectangle "Original Ticket\nSupplement same requirement" as original_ticket
rectangle "New Plan\nIndependent requirement" as new_plan

requirement --> plan : persists as
plan --> ordinary : ordinary scope
plan --> complex : distinct behavior boundaries
plan --> original_ticket : same-requirement follow-up
requirement --> new_plan : independent scope, even if prior Plan is unmerged

note bottom of plan
  Add a Ticket only for a genuine behavior boundary.
  Internal implementation steps need no separate IDs, status, or gates.
  Publication and merge occur only when authorized.
end note
@enduml
